  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Mini Western Desert has the highest temperature of Fang Yuan’s mini regions, and most of the fire path dao marks in the sovereign immortal aperture are gathered here, which is why its soil is sandy. It holds three main resource points: the eerie fire dragon python dens, the sand gull soil beach, and the rotten black swamp, formed when Fang Yuan underwent tribulation and still low in output so soon after. The beach produces sand gull soil, a Gu material that feeds connect luck Immortal Gu and that Fang Yuan now sells for immortal essence stones since he no longer holds that Gu. The rotten black swamp is thick with dark path dao marks, and he has already reworked it into a dark path Gu worm resource point. Alongside them sit two blessed lands: an earth path blessed land resembling a rotting swamp, holding five desolate beast mud monsters and managed by the small mudman land spirit, and Liu Yong’s enslavement path blessed land, holding more than twenty dog desolate beasts and managed by a black hound land spirit.",
      "chapters": [
        1291
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_connect_luck",
        "sys_gu_worms",
        "char_liu_yong"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Black hound mound, which belongs to Liu Yong blessed land and is managed by the black hound land spirit, is among the sites Fang Yuan concentrates on here. Corpse City, a mortal Gu House from Western Desert’s translocation desert, is also placed there.",
      "chapters": [
        1461
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_corpse_city",
        "sys_mortal_gu_house",
        "reg_western_desert"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inkman City occupies the desert in Mini Western Desert. Fang Yuan captures the city and moves it there. Toxic vines and windmill trees spread toward the city until reinforcements arrive, and Combat Beast King records that the Inkman City issue has been resolved.",
      "chapters": [
        2127
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "vegetation-crisis-relief",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_inkman_city",
        "char_combat_beast_king"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo Tan Sang is almost like the person in charge of Mini Western Desert. He governs Inkman City and many other locations, and stations Gu Immortals to protect residents and resource points such as white steel bowl valley, rotten swamp, and hibiscus trees when tribulation strikes.",
      "chapters": [
        2204
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "desert-governance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_mo_tan_sang",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Twelfth Hair names Mo Tan Sang the Gu Immortal leader of Mini Western Desert. A mission board entry asks for an expert when Mo Tan Sang becomes mysteriously pregnant while handling a sudden situation.",
      "chapters": [
        2242
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inkman-leadership",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_twelfth_hair"
      ]
    }
